WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:07.200
Nonprofit radio stations across the country, it was really struggling for dollars, right.

2
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:11.160
I don’t know if that’s the case with KLSU, but it was part of the climate.

3
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.940
What Darren [Gauthier] wanted to do was pay the deejays.

4
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:16.300
I mean, we were getting minimum wage or something.

5
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.280
It wasn’t lots of money.

6
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.220
But there was this idea that the students were being controlled.

7
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:26.420
The people who opposed it thought, “Oh you’re going to control the students and make them play this stuff from a computer.”

8
00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:29.260
Of course the computer is programmed by a human.

9
00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:31.820
It’s not like, you know, the singularity has occurred.

10
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:37.340
But the whole thing was controversial also because of the people who were ousted.

11
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.380
And they were all very vocal, creative people too.

12
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:47.480
So you had some people who were involved in designing stickers that made it all over, like, everyone’s cars across Baton Rouge.

13
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:48.880
And they were really cool stickers.

14
00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:54.640
They took the KLSU logo and then rearranged the letters and spelled the word “suks” S-U-K-S.

15
00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:59.040
And they were so popular on Chimes Street, and like, all over town.

16
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.340
The people who made them were designers, and they were good designers.

17
00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:06.540
And they figured out an underground way to distribute the stickers.

18
00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:10.540
I actually wrote a paper when I was in journalism school here.

19
00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:16.680
I had a professor named Matt Reavy and we had to do a story that was basically navigating a controversy.

20
00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.540
And I was like “I’m sitting right in it.”
